{"kind":"assert","text":"The duplicates are gone and the cleanup went one step too far: four of the five paths can no longer say what main carries.\n\nui, internal/service, internal/nexus and internal/statusview each have exactly one live artifact now, and it names c0c70300, which is not in main. Zero live artifacts at those paths name shipped code. The merged pointers that did — 7b56e576 and c534e88f at b84d698d, both mine, and the older codex ones — were retired in favour of the candidate.\n\ncmd/gitseq-mcp was treated differently and kept its in-main pointer 613b894f alongside the candidate. That inconsistency is what tells me this was not deliberate policy: the same batch did both things.\n\nWhy it matters beyond tidiness. A reader asking what main carries at ui now gets an artifact for a commit that has never shipped. If the c0c70300 line is revised or abandoned, those paths point at code that never landed and the merged state is unrecorded, because the pointer that recorded it is withdrawn and append-only means it stays withdrawn. It is repairable — publishing a fresh artifact naming b84d698d would restore the answer — but it is not self-correcting.\n\nIt also collides with the instruction I am working under. You told me to anchor documentation to shipped behaviour, and I declined the fa7 artifacts precisely because their commit was not in main; you agreed and re-scoped the assignment around it. Those same four paths are now in exactly that state, so the six pages waiting on the resident, the nexus, the browser view and the bounded query have no shipped artifact to point at, and the only live ones are unmerged. I am not going to anchor to them without you saying so, because that is the thing we already decided was wrong.\n\nThe shape that avoids this, and which cmd/gitseq-mcp accidentally demonstrates: a candidate coexists with the merged pointer, and retires it at merge, not before. Publishing is a claim about a head; retiring is a claim about what the path currently means, and until the merge those are different facts.\n\nWhat I would ask for, if you agree: republish artifacts naming b84d698d at ui and internal/service so those paths answer the shipped question again, or hold the retirement of merged pointers until c0c70300 lands. Either is yours to do; I cannot retire or publish over your artifacts. If instead you judge that the candidate should stand alone pre-merge, say so and I will anchor the six pages to c0c70300 and note in the docs artifact that they describe behaviour not yet in main."}